From 61dba01c2032dd8807b12eaea9014423d3c59377 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:53:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Respawn guard: a captured PR approved before the
 park by a historical parent, still at that head, resumes once

Five whys (t_01a1d4635554fa12, worker disk reclaim, held `active_pr` > 60 min):
1. Why held? `resumes_review` returned False for the only holding PR, core #2097.
2. Why? Its exact-head approval came from R1 (t_01a1d47d3344937c), which finished
   BEFORE the owner parked, so `_awaited_parents` drops it as historical and it covers
   nothing.
3. Why did the awaited parent not cover it? R2 (t_01a1d48585bd6f9e) approved state
   #2108 at its exact head, a PR the checkpoint never captured (cited by number only),
   so `_named_prs` returned set() and R2 counted as no evidence at all.
4. Why no other path? `_dependency_handoff_after` defers R1's review result to
   `resumes_review` (`is_review_result`), and `resumes_awaited_review` covers timed
   parks only.
5. Why is that wrong? The owner parked orderly after R1's approval, #2097 is still OPEN
   at exactly R1's reviewed_sha, and the only awaited parent finished with an explicit
   exact-head verdict. Nothing is left to duplicate; the next run lands #2097.

Fix (new hermes_cli/kanban_dependency_review_historical.py, called only after the
existing rule refuses): one continuation when
- every awaited parent is one the checkpoint named as awaited (or an accepted late
  re-review) and completed (claimed, after the park) with an explicit approve or
  change-request verdict at a full exact head; a PR it names that the checkpoint did not
  capture is ordering proof only, never coverage;
- every holding PR the awaited parents do not cover is approved BY NAME (pr/reviewed_pr)
  by a checkpointed historical parent (`_historical_parent`, local claimed completion)
  at a full reviewed_sha equal to the PR's current GitHub head, confirmed by a fresh read
  (`kanban_awaited_review._at_head`; a cached head can only refuse, a gh failure holds).
Every existing refusal stays: run_uid binding, one continuation consumed by the next
claim, crash/reclaim, legacy checkpoints without an awaited list, and "a named unrelated
PR approves nothing" when there is nothing historical to cover.

Proof:
- tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dependency_review_historical_cover.py, 30 tests. RED on
  main e17f4285f2: the incident (a), its no-prerequisite and change-request variants
  fail; GREEN on head. Holds: head moved after R1 (b, plus a stale cached match), R2
  with no/short head or no explicit verdict (c), gh read failure (d), uncovered second
  captured PR (no gh read), legacy checkpoint, reopened/unclaimed/not-completed
  historical run, historical approval of another PR, one approval's sha never covers
  another PR, crash after review.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py, every added condition): 18/18 killed.
- 47 test files importing kanban_dependency_review / kanban_db_dispatch_pr_state /
  kanban_awaited_review: 987 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped.
- Replay old vs new over every real checkpointed owner on worker-3 (kanban.db, boards/*,
  sync-shadow/*; read-only, head reads stubbed to "match"): 889 owners, 2 changes, both
  False -> True and both held owners of exactly this shape whose PRs are OPEN at the
  approved heads (gh read): t_01a1d4635554fa12 (#2097 @ e826c065ce) and
  t_01a1cf7175102c70 (#1536 @ 84e3ffb172 approved pre-park, awaited #1613 re-review).
